#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §4.5 Observation axioms — hemodynamic warm-up requirement.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A BOLD signal is produced by convolving simulated neural activity
# with a hemodynamic response function (HRF) of finite support. The
# convolution is causal: BOLD at time t is a weighted sum of neural
# activity over the preceding kernel window, so the first kernel-length
# of the recorded signal depends on activity from *before* recording
# starts. The integrator supplies that pre-roll from the discarded
# transient (`tvbo:transient_time`). If the transient is shorter than
# the HRF kernel, the convolution history buffer is under-filled, the
# valid-mode output is truncated, and its time axis shifts earlier —
# the BOLD then spuriously *precedes* the stimulus instead of lagging
# it by the hemodynamic delay. OWL cannot state the numeric inequality;
# it is documented here as an axiom and enforced in `tvb-o.shacl.ttl`.
#

tvbo:HemodynamicObservation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf tvbo:Observation ;
    rdfs:label "Hemodynamic observation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An observation model that maps neural activity to a haemodynamic / BOLD signal by causal convolution with a finite-support HRF kernel."@en .

<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_double_exponential> a tvbo:HemodynamicObservation .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma>              a tvbo:HemodynamicObservation .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas>  a tvbo:HemodynamicObservation .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi>         a tvbo:HemodynamicObservation .

tvbo:hrfKernelDuration a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tvbo:HemodynamicObservation ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label  "HRF kernel duration (ms)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Temporal support of the HRF convolution kernel, in milliseconds; the lower bound the simulated transient must satisfy."@en .

tvbo:HemodynamicWarmupRequirement a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hemodynamic warm-up requirement"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Modelling axiom: for any tvbo:HemodynamicObservation, the discarded transient (tvbo:transient_time) MUST be ≥ the observation's HRF kernel duration (tvbo:hrfKernelDuration). Otherwise the causal HRF convolution is under-filled and the BOLD time axis shifts earlier, so the signal spuriously precedes the stimulus rather than lagging it by the hemodynamic delay. Example: the tvboptim BOLD pipeline uses a 20000 ms kernel (5000 samples at dt = 4 ms) via prepend_history + valid-mode convolution, so transient_time ≥ 20000 ms is required."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso tvbo:HemodynamicObservation, tvbo:hrfKernelDuration, tvbo:transient_time ;
    skos:scopeNote "Observed empirically (TVB-O acoustic-stimulation use-case, 2026): a 15000 ms transient (< 20000 ms kernel) made auditory BOLD precede the loudness by ~1 s with a mislabelled 1043 ms TR; transient ≥ 20000 ms restored a causal hemodynamic lag (≈ +1.5 s) and the correct 1000 ms TR."@en .

